  "question": {
    "text": "The relative error in the determination of the surface area of a sphere is $\\alpha$. Then the relative error in the determination of its volume is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3fLa0",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3} \\alpha$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UdcHF",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3} \\alpha$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ghcqb",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{2} \\alpha$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6nvNY",
      "text": "\n$\\alpha$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Relative error in Surface area, $\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{s}}{\\mathrm{s}}=2 \\times \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{r}}{\\mathrm{r}}=\\alpha$ and relative error in volume, $\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{v}}{\\mathrm{v}}=3 \\times \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{r}}{\\mathrm{r}}$\n$\\therefore$ Relative error in volume w.r.t. relative error in area,\n$$\n\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{v}}{\\mathrm{v}}=\\frac{3}{2} \\alpha\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
